<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15149" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρι-φρᾰδής</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράζομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clear,
				manifest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.326
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέα . . ἀριφραδέα
			τέτυκται</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				240
			</span></i>: so poet.Adv.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δέως</span>
			<i>plainly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀγορεύει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.176
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>clear to the sight, bright,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				24.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>very thoughtful, wise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				347
			</span></i> (as cited by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				135.25
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
